=== Image Caption Logic Breakdown ===
The template builds the image caption in a very specific order. It checks for parameters one by one, and as soon as it finds one, it uses it and ignores the rest in the main caption group.

==== Main Caption Priority ====
The template follows this hierarchy to generate the main part of the caption:
# <code>imagedescr</code>: This provides a fully custom caption and overrides all other main caption parameters.
# <code>imagesong</code>: If no <code>imagedescr</code>, this generates a caption about a song cover. It uses <code>songfeat</code> and <code>gender</code> (...his/her/their cover of...) to add detail.
# <code>imagegroup</code>: If the first two are missing, this generates a caption about the group the person is seen with.
# <code>otherillustrator</code>: The lowest priority option, used for non-official art.

==== Caption Add-on ====
* <code>officialillustrator</code>: This parameter is independent. If this parameter is filled, its text will always be appended to the end of the generated caption, regardless of which other parameters were used.

==== Parameter Relationships & Incompatibilities ====
This table summarizes how the parameters interact:
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Interacts With
! Incompatible With (Will be ignored if...)
|-
| <code>imagedescr</code>
| <code>officialillustrator</code> (which appends to it)
| <code>imagesong</code>, <code>songfeat</code>, <code>imagegroup</code>, and <code>otherillustrator</code> are all hidden.
|-
| <code>imagesong</code>
| <code>songfeat</code>, <code>gender</code>, <code>officialillustrator</code>
| <code>imagedescr</code> is present.
|-
| <code>imagegroup</code>
| <code>officialillustrator</code>
| <code>imagedescr</code> or <code>imagesong</code> are present.
|-
| <code>otherillustrator</code>
| <code>officialillustrator</code>
| <code>imagedescr</code>, <code>imagesong</code>, or <code>imagegroup</code> are present.
|-
| <code>officialillustrator</code>
| '''Everything.''' It always appends itself.
| Nothing.
|-
| <code>songfeat</code>
| <code>imagesong</code> (relies on it)
| <code>imagesong</code> is not present.
|}
